## Context

I am the lead architect for a **Tungsten TotalAgility hybrid deployment** at AIB, a regulated Irish financial institution. The deployment model is:

- **TTA SaaS tenant** hosts the process engine, AI/OCR pipeline, document classification, field extraction, job state machine, worker queues, and document store
- **Four dedicated on-premises Integration Servers** (Windows Server) connected to the SaaS tenant via outbound HTTPS only:
  - IS-1: Email ingestion — monitors Exchange mailboxes, creates TTA jobs via Job API, uploads document content
  - IS-2: Folder/UNC ingestion — hot folder scanning, creates TTA jobs via Job API
  - IS-3: ECM export — Core Worker polls ECMExport worker group, fetches documents from SaaS, calls IBM CM8 Resource Manager on LAN
  - IS-4: DB integration — Core Worker polls DBIntegration worker group, executes DB2/Oracle lookups and writes on LAN
- All IS-to-SaaS communication is outbound HTTPS port 443. The SaaS tenant never initiates inbound connections to any IS.
- Worker group assignment happens at process design time in TTA Designer. Steps assigned to a named worker group are only claimable by an IS registered to that group.
- The platform is being built as a migration target from **Kofax Capture**, handling document capture, OCR, IDP, and export to IBM CM8 ECM.
- Use cases include: email ingestion with PDF attachments, folder-based batch scanning, document classification and field extraction in the cloud, followed by IS-side ECM export with AI-inferred document type used as CM8 metadata.
- IBM BAW is also deployed at AIB and forms part of the broader orchestration layer outside of TTA's scope.

